# No player gets priority in the untap step (CR 502.4), but an effect "for as long as this creature remains tapped" ends
# the moment Old Man of the Sea untaps (CR 611.2b), not at the next check of state-based actions. Bot1's Old Man has taken
# Bot2's Dark Confidant; in Bot1's next untap step Bot1 untaps Old Man, so when Bot1's upkeep begins the Confidant is Bot2's
# again and its "at the beginning of your upkeep" ability does not trigger for Bot1 (CR 503.1a, 603.2): Bot1 does not reveal
# the Lightning Bolt on top of its library or lose 1 life for it, and draws the Bolt in its draw step instead.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Mox Jet
Island
Old Man of the Sea
Island
Island
Island
Island
Lightning Bolt
Island x11

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Dark Confidant
Swamp x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Old Man of the Sea.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Dark Confidant.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Old Man of the Sea.Activate(Bot2.Battlefield.Dark Confidant)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Dark Confidant.Power = 2
Bot1.Accept
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Old Man of the Sea.Tapped = false

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot1.Hand = Island; Island; Island; Island; Lightning Bolt
Bot2.Battlefield = Swamp; Mox Jet; Dark Confidant
